          "know": {
            "baseline": "Workspaces with a second active person within 7 days. Not supplied. Measure it for four weeks before launch.",
            "expect": "Rises. The smallest lift worth shipping is 2 points on this measure. That is a decision threshold, not an estimate of the result.",
            "stop": "Paid conversion within 30 days falls, unwanted-invite reports rise, or workspaces that turn sharing off rise, against the control group."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "1.2",
          "title": "Admins cannot see what a guest will see",
          "problem": "4 of 8 interviewees kept private notes or drafts in the workspace and could not tell what an invitee would see. They had no way to preview it, and 3 of the 4 were asked about it directly, so the weight is lower than the count.",
          "change": "Show a Preview as guest step before the link is made. It draws the page exactly as a view-only guest gets it.",
          "why": "A preview in a different role from the one given would repeat the mismatch seen in Halyard.",
          "constraint": {
            "label": "Risk from the pre-mortem",
            "text": "R1: admins share before the workspace is ready. A preview shows the page but does not change when the admin feels ready, so 2.1 carries the timing."
          },
