    {
      "n": 2,
      "id": "ask",
      "title": "When to ask, and what it costs",
      "summary": "Offer sharing once there is something to show, and say what a seat costs.",
      "lead": "Sharing is offered after the first project has three items, not during signup. The invite dialog says what a member seat costs.",
      "points": [
        {
          "id": "2.1",
          "title": "Nothing offers sharing while the plan takes shape",
          "problem": "The invite is the last row of the Home checklist, has no button, and the project page never mentions another person. 6 of 8 interviewees held the plan back until it looked presentable.",
          "change": "When a project has three items, show a card above the table that reads 'Ready to show someone?' with a Share button. Do not ask during signup.",
          "why": "Waiting for the plan to look ready is the main reason for delay, so the ask belongs after there is something to show.",
          "constraint": {
            "label": "Risk from the pre-mortem",
            "text": "R1: a card can nudge an admin to share too early. The card sends nothing. It opens the preview from 1.2 first."
          },
