    {
      "n": 3,
      "id": "guest",
      "title": "The guest's side",
      "summary": "The guest lands on the page and can ask to edit.",
      "lead": "What the person who only looks sees, and how a guest becomes a paid member.",
      "points": [
        {
          "id": "3.1",
          "title": "Nothing connects looking at a plan to paying for a seat",
          "problem": "Corbel guests can look but have no way to join, so none becomes a paid seat. Larkspur has no guest at all, and billing for a guest who becomes a member is not designed.",
          "change": "Put an Ask to edit button on the shared page. The admin gets the request and approves it, and the seat is paid for at that moment, with the cost shown.",
          "why": "Paying only when someone needs to edit keeps the first look free and still reaches a paid seat.",
          "constraint": {
            "label": "Dependency",
            "text": "The billing for a guest who becomes a member is not designed. This point cannot ship until the billing owner designs it. Pre-mortem R6 warns that free guests may never become paid seats."
          },
          "evidence": [
